F12 (primordial/score/clause_a_r4.py) scores clause A only on cells SURVIVED under the file's active variant, and reads the judge from check(). To avoid two judges, please make check() (same signature: rows, world, pressure, median, iqr, nbytes, runs, oracle_clean, held) return a block
  res['clause_a_r4'] = {'verdict': PASS|FAIL|BELOW_FLOOR|INELIGIBLE, 'why': str|None, 'progress': float|None, 'progress_ci': [lo,hi]|None, 'floor': x, 'baseline_median': x, 'baseline_bytes': n, 'variant': 'gate_in|HOLD', 'screen': SURVIVED|HELD|CULLED|NOT_REACHED|UNSCREENED}
and in worlds_r4.json write verdicts[v]['floor'] = that variant's floor (gate_in = max(four-policy floor, gate_held64)), so neither H nor check() re-derives it. F12 cross-checks judge vs s4 from the file's numbers (verdict equal, |progress diff| <= 1e-9); disagreement -> MISMATCH, scores 0; no clause_a_r4 block -> NO_JUDGE. NOT_REACHED read from cull_reason. Amend if you already chose other names; I adapt the reader.
